/-!
# The placed quadratic actor on the actual component seed spans

When H is generated by the Sylow orbit of a relative component and T,
perfectness identifies that orbit with O²(H). The placed F.9.16 actor is
therefore faithful on this component orbit. The genuine homogeneous seed
from Seeds and the source span theorem supply the same quadratic actor,
with its cubic bound, on every intermediate orbit span. The T-span is the
full H-span, and F.9.18(6) gives exhaustion or its precise FF alternatives.

The terminal application proves the generation premise on J=⟨K^T⟩T,
inside the unchanged Mc. Its space is U_J/Z; no equality U_J=U_Mc is
asserted. Seeds separately constructs the D.3 input on the full U_Mc/Z.
The remaining FF exclusions, natural-module recognition and terminal
assembly stay with qt-e-suitable-component-supports. Original 14.6.18
remains with qt-e-14625-source.
Source: Aschbacher--Smith F.9.18(1--3,6), printed pp.325--326;
14.6.20--22, printed pp.1037--1038.
-/

public section
